---
title: "vesca_lock - Lock SCA for veSCA (Scallop Lend)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_amount: check sca_amount > 0
    q_check_amount --> q_error_amount: sca_amount == 0
    q_error_amount --> [*]: abort error
    q_check_amount --> q_check_duration: sca_amount > 0
    q_check_duration --> q_error_duration: lock_rounds < 1 or lock_rounds > 1460
    q_error_duration --> [*]: abort error (invalid lock duration)
    q_check_duration --> q_check_unlock_time: 1 <= lock_rounds <= 1460
    q_check_unlock_time --> q_error_unlock: unlock_date not at 12AM UTC boundary
    q_error_unlock --> [*]: abort error (invalid unlock date)
    q_check_unlock_time --> q_check_full_round: unlock_date at 12AM UTC
    q_check_full_round --> q_error_round: lock period < 1 full round (24h)
    q_error_round --> [*]: abort error (less than 1 full round)
    q_check_full_round --> q_calc_vesca: lock period >= 1 full round
    q_calc_vesca --> q_lock: vesca_amount = sca_amount * (remain_lock_period / 4_years)
    q_lock --> q_transfer_sca: lock sca_amount in veSCA contract
    q_transfer_sca --> [*]: return veSCA position with decay schedule

    note right of q_calc_vesca
        INV-001: veSCA = SCA * (RemainLockPeriod / 4Years)
        INV-002: veSCA decays linearly to 0 at unlock_date
        INV-003: max lock = 1460 rounds = 4 years
        INV-004: min lock = 1 full round (24 hours from next 12AM UTC)
    end note

    note right of q_lock
        INV-005: locked SCA is 100% recoverable after lock expires
        INV-006: users can extend lock period (never shorten)
        INV-007: increasing SCA stake refreshes veSCA amount
    end note
